==Battleground==
*5 [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 6~8 seconds<sup>180f~240f</sup>.
*1 [[Heavenly Hippoe]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 30~33.33 seconds<sup>900f~1,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Deathkory]] spawns as the boss.
**3 [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn, delay 36.67~40 seconds<sup>1,100f~1,200f</sup>.
**1 [[Boraphim]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Start the stage by leveling up your wallet and keeping the Heavenly Hippoe alive as long as possible. After hitting the base, lure Boraphim to your base, then use stallers like [[Juliet Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Juliet]] and try to rush Boraphim down before Deathkory gets to the frontline. 

[[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N110 (Rare Cat)|Farmboy Cat]] both work great against Boraphim, and their [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]] prevents them from getting immediately deleted by Deathkory. Additionally, [[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel Cat]] can help with piercing Deathkory's shield; while they lack Wave Immunity, their resistance against Aku means that they don't take much damage from his waves in practice.

